A||||3||Fierozilla||Clutch problem FIXED!!! Discovered the strange problem.||||10||
Z||000000||Fierozilla||10-28-2001||06:50 PM||||Well I was sweating this one. After ordering a new steel clutch pedal and then getting an email stating it was discontinued, I began to worry. After closer inspection however, I noticed my pedal <I>seemed</I> fine..didnt look bent anywhere, sat well above the break pedal, ect.<BR>Anyhow I had a friend check the travel on the slave while I pressed in the clutch..heres what I <I>didnt</I> expect. My friend tells me he sees the problem. He goes to push in the clutch as I watch the slave cylinder and low and behold, a bolt that holds the slave cylinder in place was loose! Whenever the clutch pedal was pushed, the entire slave cylinder moved about half an inch! Needless to say I tightened it up. <BR>Well, that pretty much fixed it, but it still was quite right. So we go to bleed the system. EEK!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I get about 1/2 an inch in the bottle of this pasty black goo....NOT good! We bled the system for a while, ran new fluid through it until all the air was out and only new, clean fluid came through, then topped it off.<BR>Voila! She shifts like a brand new car again! <I>PHEW!!!</I><BR>So for those of you w/ the classic clutch wont engange problem, you just never know..it may be something as simple as that!||||reg||10
Z||000001||MrPBody||10-28-2001||09:05 PM||||Congrats!  I'm glad <I>someone</I> fixed his clutch, even if I haven't.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-28-2001||09:43 PM||||Im a firm believer in keeping all the fluids in a car constantly fresh. Always helps in making your car last longer!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||lou_dias||10-28-2001||11:54 PM||||a couple of months ago, my pedal wouldn't lift then sometimes I had excessive pressure, turned out to be the spring in the master broke into a few pieces and when the lined up a certain way, it would come up fine but be hard to push down and other times it would be ok or very bad.<P>My buddy took apart my master and found the spring broken and replaced it with 2 springs from Suzuki bikes and I have light pressure and full pedal movement and clutch en/disengagement.<P>each spring was half the length but the same width of the fiero spring.<P>works great!||||reg||1
